title: 2. Why one author, and which
pid: 7e77cd23-2f2d-4596-87f2-8448acaa834a
body: |2-
  A plan is where the decisions become explicit, and two authors make
  two sets of them. The hardest decision is usually the one-way door
  from step 1. The author reads the other territories' maps in their
  graphs; where a map does not answer, it asks (the rule for a second
  specialist says how). Top does not write plans: Top does not read
  code, and costs the most. If no territory holds the hardest decision
  (a request about how the team works, say), Top names the author by
  the way of seeing it most needs.
  Rests on: read (Cognition: one thread of decisions, and a helper
  that only answers a question is safe; Brooks: conceptual integrity).
  Ours: the choice of owner, and that Top does not author, departing
  from Anthropic's research system, where the lead plans.
